  "id": "moog-little-phatty",
  "name": "Moog Little Phatty",
  "manufacturer": "Moog",
  "family": "Phatty",
  "status": "experimental",
  "trust": "local",
  "description": "Moog Little Phatty Stage II analog synthesizer: the MIDI CC table of its manual, with the value tables it points to.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "type": "manual",
      "title": "LP Stage II User's Manual",
      "notes": "MIDI CC table (pages 54, 55) read by tools/profiles/moog/read-moog-pdf.mjs from Little_Phatty_Manual.pdf (sha256 f9ae474cd83a93bd582b9a1ff928f6d85e7698ef2964da056d72659deb30b1b4), https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/Moog/LittlePhatty/Little_Phatty_Manual.pdf. Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
    }
  ],
  "testedWith": [],
  "authoringNotes": [
    "Generated by tools/profiles/moog/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/moog/synths/, not this file.",
    "Every parameter is a row of the manual's MIDI tables, with its printed name. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
    "No identity check: the manual prints no Device Inquiry reply.",
    "Ten rows print a name another row of their section has (WAVE, OCTAVE, ATTACK …); each is named here from its function column (`Sets the waveform of oscillator 2`, `Adjusts the filter envelope attack time`).",
    "The Arpeggiator Clock Rate is two controllers, CC 4 in steps of 3 BPM and CC 36 in tenths (the table's note 2); the profile has CC 4.",
    "2 knob(s) are 14-bit, 0 - 16383: the MSB and the LSB the table prints, sent in that order: CUTOFF (CC 19, LSB 51); MOD WHEEL (CC 1, LSB 33).",
    "Left out, printed without a controller (a panel switch, or `Varies`): MASTER (CC -), PRESET (CC -), CURSOR (CC -), ENTER (CC -), OCTAVE UP (CC -), OCTAVE DOWN (CC -)."
  ],
  "variables": {
    "channel": 1
  },
